#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497429} :activity/id #uuid "4b16e189-7cae-52c7-b4b2-a5ce8c27642e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049196 :topic/id #uuid "e289a183-5534-5388-8ee7-3fc0d8f4ee68" :topic/math-academy-id 1833} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497429 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335734 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0654fbb0-4464-57df-b997-793b4d140585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333048} {:answer/id #uuid "5118678c-2f8f-5690-b6fc-bf8555ce98e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333728} {:answer/id #uuid "7651226e-fce4-5b52-bc1a-76607be7511d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334058} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4a2192-9402-508c-9568-f3777b5cf2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334100} {:answer/id #uuid "a9569df6-5bae-5e8a-824f-b880322a1e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334472}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333728} :answer-field/id #uuid "25483b54-8d2f-5ef1-a991-a9c7271a8af6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b6d968e1-179a-5b9e-896d-829a90d9d8fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-64680" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)}^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3t))+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\sqrt{(9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}+(-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\sqrt{{9}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡3t+{cos}^{2}⁡3t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\,}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "295eca98-5a56-59b6-be3f-1a7e5fc824dc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497462}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497447 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5063f8a0-899b-5e4f-b70e-5fbeab173e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496834} {:answer/id #uuid "cf933d00-1cd0-58a3-b054-9a9b5f189803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497086} {:answer/id #uuid "df8562cf-2270-52ce-9299-2a3db48074d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497137} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e14dc5-18ed-5023-8fe2-0751bffc21d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497158} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3568be-b178-5f3b-b7ec-36b1e63a80e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497204}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497137} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6ba6fef-e5a6-577a-86ab-a507607e574c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f8afba66-d1aa-558e-99f9-1c7592f06bb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131232" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,2\\sqrt{2}t,\\,4⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}⟨4t,\\,\\sqrt{2}(4-{t}^{2}),\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(4t)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}(4-{t}^{2}))}^{2}+(-4t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+2{(4-{t}^{2})}^{2}+16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+(32-16{t}^{2}+2{t}^{4})+16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{t}^{4}+16{t}^{2}+32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2({t}^{2}+4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{{t}^{2}+4} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2})}^{2}+{(2\\sqrt{2}t)}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+8{t}^{2}+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{{t}^{2}+4})}{{t}^{2}+4}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{({t}^{2}+4)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7996da4d-65c7-519a-8f8a-fbfe32a74aa7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497455}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497455 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb19a9f-9048-5bd2-9825-48b46c374012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263819} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b9851-e23d-5c89-85c7-166c2502e4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263923} {:answer/id #uuid "792aef7e-fcea-560d-8fb8-5bfd5fef2507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264051} {:answer/id #uuid "d64da940-c21b-5ec2-8ac3-b32049952204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264863} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb74e9b-1c1a-510f-8253-e0339f0362f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265089}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265089} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc15e45-edbf-58cf-997c-64f5fe6f3649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c55df30b-b976-5e8f-92e6-7035630c5b16" :question/math-academy-id "q-131931" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3}⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le 4\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8c342d34-2861-5edd-8ee3-b1b129ac8611"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497462 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099529b2-f2d8-571a-8051-1abe76e80e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345427} {:answer/id #uuid "1c89dd2c-b2a6-55ce-9cde-64a9db39f22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345598} {:answer/id #uuid "2af3437a-013c-5c2c-ba66-e91d3d0b3776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345732} {:answer/id #uuid "e08432ed-6cab-5f33-bc9d-ccb5e07f25a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347321} {:answer/id #uuid "e22f899c-983b-59f9-b450-dbd732e6a167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345732} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5bdbcf-f249-5c99-b7cb-71c1723c6391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19bd97de-146f-5b50-9592-8b78d39231d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-80523" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩,\\,0\\le s<10\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{5}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a52d7a0f-ae82-55ee-b781-f303b31787d0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497471}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497471 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1251bed4-415d-5590-a871-e4a9657e13d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433617} {:answer/id #uuid "481e6b9f-c5af-58b8-b98e-c12965a43b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433619} {:answer/id #uuid "c86e68ce-7275-5906-ac2f-57213bf72bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433622} {:answer/id #uuid "d87a76ef-7c66-5822-bbbd-0695f641dc2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433623} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a5693f-64fa-5920-9519-f34d893234c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433625}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433622} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef00e22-7033-5539-a4d7-5c70d771c4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c48a3e25-1a31-5723-bb94-d587dcc4bb55" :question/math-academy-id "q-80546" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${T}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+16{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,2\\,}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bc2db5d0-2c5f-5532-ae92-9e8a5ca14fe2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497447}}] :activity/title "Introduction to Curvature" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496647}]}
